+# Bun migration
+
+Requires Bun 1.4.4. Install dependencies with `bun install --frozen-lockfile`.
+Use `bun run run -- <operation> <path> [text]` for the CLI,
+`bun run typecheck` for strict TypeScript checking, and `bun run check` for
+the previous check entry point. Run regression checks with `bun test`.
+The original project had no serve, test, or build task; no build is required.
+
+File operations now use Node-compatible filesystem APIs. Exclusive creation
+uses `wx`, replacement still truncates or creates, and missing-file detection
+handles only `ENOENT`. Directory listings still exclude directories and symlinks
+and sort filenames. UTF-8 decoding preserves the BOM and replaces malformed
+UTF-8, matching the original runtime. Child execution uses the current
+Bun executable with an absolute source path, collecting stdout and stderr
+concurrently while retaining the child's exit status.
+
+Bun does not implement Deno's permission sandbox. The former run task granted
+read, write, and subprocess access; Bun additionally has the process user's
+normal environment and network access. Use an OS sandbox if isolation is
+required. Runtime exception names, stack traces, and diagnostic formatting
+can differ; failed operations still fail without swallowing unrelated errors.
+
+There were no application dependencies to migrate. TypeScript 7.0.2 and
+@types/bun 1.4.4 are exact development dependencies, locked in bun.lock.
+Deno configuration and execution have been removed. Formatting/linting
+replacement and broad reformatting are intentionally out of scope.
